WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.340 --> 00:00:02.074
I couldn't even get cast as an Italian,

00:00:02.074 --> 00:00:04.522
I'll never forget where
there was a party scene,

00:00:04.522 --> 00:00:07.913
is this 300 guests, (laughing) I said no.

00:00:07.913 --> 00:00:11.469
But the fear is the fuel that
we use for overachievement.

00:00:11.469 --> 00:00:14.842
If I wasn't afraid at times,
I wouldn't work as hard.

00:00:14.842 --> 00:00:17.422
You've got to take chances,
you've got to gamble,

00:00:17.422 --> 00:00:20.408
and if you win 51% of the
time, you've got it made.

00:00:20.408 --> 00:00:23.617
- He's an American actor,
filmmaker and screenwriter.

00:00:23.617 --> 00:00:26.303
He's best known for his
roles as Rocky Balboa,

00:00:26.303 --> 00:00:27.855
and John Rambo.

00:00:27.855 --> 00:00:30.646
Philadelphia also has a
statue of his Rocky character

00:00:30.646 --> 00:00:33.147
permanently placed by the Museum of Art.

00:00:33.147 --> 00:00:35.178
He's Sylvester Stallone,
and here's my take

00:00:35.178 --> 00:00:38.032
on his Top Ten Rules
for Success, volume two.

00:00:38.032 --> 00:00:39.790
Rule number one is my personal favorite,

00:00:39.790 --> 00:00:42.033
and I'd love to know which
one you guys like the best.

00:00:42.033 --> 00:00:43.407
And as always as you're watching,

00:00:43.407 --> 00:00:45.398
if you hear something that
really resonates with you,

00:00:45.398 --> 00:00:47.023
please leave it in the comments below,

00:00:47.023 --> 00:00:48.678
put quotes around it so other people

00:00:48.678 --> 00:00:51.276
can be inspired as well,
and when you write it down,

00:00:51.276 --> 00:00:54.338
it's much more likely to
stick with you as well.

00:00:54.338 --> 00:00:55.171
Enjoy!

00:00:58.080 --> 00:01:01.080
(high energy music)

00:01:08.151 --> 00:01:10.333
- I truly believe, and
people throw the word around,

00:01:10.333 --> 00:01:13.401
dreams, it's all about
dreams, and by the way,

00:01:13.401 --> 00:01:15.575
dreams cost nothing, they're free.

00:01:15.575 --> 00:01:18.257
The hard part is just keeping them going,

00:01:18.257 --> 00:01:21.039
and please keep them
going because we're here

00:01:21.039 --> 00:01:24.059
for one simple reason,
he believed in the dream,

00:01:24.059 --> 00:01:26.761
I believed in the dream,
and our dreams come true,

00:01:26.761 --> 00:01:30.049
and there's no reason every
one of yours can't either.

00:01:30.049 --> 00:01:30.882
Thank you very much.

00:01:30.882 --> 00:01:31.859
(audience applauds)

00:01:31.859 --> 00:01:33.699
- Let's start from the beginning.

00:01:33.699 --> 00:01:36.267
Was there ever a time
that you doubted yourself?

00:01:36.267 --> 00:01:39.539
- Yeah, you know I
thought, when I lived in

00:01:39.539 --> 00:01:43.045
basically this flophouse, it's
$26 a week, very transient,

00:01:43.045 --> 00:01:45.348
and you shared a floor with 10 people,

00:01:45.348 --> 00:01:47.695
you don't know anybody on
the plan, literally no one.

00:01:47.695 --> 00:01:50.522
- I think I recall you saying,
you're acting at one point,

00:01:50.522 --> 00:01:52.786
The Godfather, and you said
you couldn't even get in a...

00:01:52.786 --> 00:01:56.006
- (laughing) I couldn't
even get cast as an Italian,

00:01:56.006 --> 00:01:58.332
I never forget where
there was a party scene,

00:01:58.332 --> 00:02:02.146
is this 300 guests? (laughing) I said no.

00:02:02.146 --> 00:02:04.046
I go, what part of me didn't make it

00:02:04.046 --> 00:02:07.418
past the Italian identification aspect,

00:02:07.418 --> 00:02:10.861
he goes, eh, I don't know,
you just don't fit in,

00:02:10.861 --> 00:02:11.694
I went, wow,

00:02:11.694 --> 00:02:14.161
God's telling me something.
- That's got to (laughing)

00:02:14.161 --> 00:02:15.535
- That's got to play with
your psyche a little bit!

00:02:15.535 --> 00:02:17.256
- Little bit.
- I don't know.

00:02:17.256 --> 00:02:18.974
But it didn't, and you decided

00:02:18.974 --> 00:02:23.141
to take matters into your
own hands, by writing Rocky.

00:02:24.205 --> 00:02:26.417
- Y'know, I been comin'
here for six years,

00:02:26.417 --> 00:02:27.748
six years you been stickin' it to me,

00:02:27.748 --> 00:02:29.037
I want to know how come.

00:02:29.037 --> 00:02:29.870
- You want to know?

00:02:29.870 --> 00:02:31.169
- I want to know!

00:02:31.169 --> 00:02:33.168
- Okay I'm going to tell ya!

00:02:33.168 --> 00:02:36.063
'Cause you had the talent
to become a good fighter,

00:02:36.063 --> 00:02:38.849
and instead of that, you
became a lane breaker.

00:02:38.849 --> 00:02:42.710
- You were able to write Rocky
in three and a half days.

00:02:42.710 --> 00:02:45.736
The movie that went on to be Best Picture,

00:02:45.736 --> 00:02:47.194
you wrote in three and a half days?

00:02:47.194 --> 00:02:48.110
- Yes, yes.

00:02:48.110 --> 00:02:48.986
- Was it just flowing out of you?

00:02:48.986 --> 00:02:50.867
- In a way it was, I knew that this

00:02:50.867 --> 00:02:52.167
was going to be very flawed,

00:02:52.167 --> 00:02:54.228
but if I could get from
the beginning to the end,

00:02:54.228 --> 00:02:56.637
with some semblance of a character,

00:02:56.637 --> 00:02:59.298
then I'll repair the rest along the way.

00:02:59.298 --> 00:03:03.049
- And you want to star in
it, and you're told no,

00:03:03.049 --> 00:03:05.432
you were even offered $250,000--

00:03:05.432 --> 00:03:06.551
- 360.

00:03:06.551 --> 00:03:08.581
- 360, you're a struggling actor.

00:03:08.581 --> 00:03:09.414
- Ooh...

00:03:09.414 --> 00:03:10.940
- You can't make ends meet.
- No.

00:03:10.940 --> 00:03:12.397
- You're getting offerred all this money,

00:03:12.397 --> 00:03:14.519
but you didn't take it.

00:03:14.519 --> 00:03:17.485
- No, I just didn't understand
how the rules of life

00:03:17.485 --> 00:03:21.729
were played at that point, but
this character, I understood.

00:03:21.729 --> 00:03:24.637
If I had to rewind the clock ten years,

00:03:24.637 --> 00:03:28.804
I would have insisted, by people
that were close to me, that

00:03:31.010 --> 00:03:34.411
please, push me into very unsafe projects,

00:03:34.411 --> 00:03:37.146
at least every other one.

00:03:37.146 --> 00:03:40.688
I think it's professionally responsible

00:03:40.688 --> 00:03:44.855
to not continue to remake the
same film over and over again,

00:03:45.761 --> 00:03:47.227
you know, what's tonight?

00:03:47.227 --> 00:03:49.372
Turkey TV dinner, turkey TV dinner...

00:03:49.372 --> 00:03:51.300
There's always fear, and
I even put it in Rocky II,

00:03:51.300 --> 00:03:54.204
that he's, "I'm afraid, I'm afraid."

00:03:54.204 --> 00:03:57.657
But the fear is the fuel that
we use for overachievement.

00:03:57.657 --> 00:04:01.991
If I wasn't afraid at times,
I wouldn't work as hard,

00:04:01.991 --> 00:04:04.330
'cause the fear is, I don't
want to sit back in mediocrity,

00:04:04.330 --> 00:04:07.313
I don't want to to just say,
I want to rest on my laurels,

00:04:07.313 --> 00:04:10.162
so I hear footsteps all the time,

00:04:10.162 --> 00:04:12.845
and I know that I only have
a certain amount of time

00:04:12.845 --> 00:04:13.728
and I don't want to waste it,

00:04:13.728 --> 00:04:16.311
because it's gone so quickly,

00:04:16.311 --> 00:04:18.978
since Rocky it's been almost
seven and a half, eight years,

00:04:18.978 --> 00:04:22.461
I think that Don and I are
just overachievers because

00:04:22.461 --> 00:04:27.194
we know that there's only a
certain amount of productivity

00:04:27.194 --> 00:04:29.330
in a day and we don't want to waste it.

00:04:29.330 --> 00:04:33.758
I am at the whims of the
character that I play,

00:04:33.758 --> 00:04:36.813
that's who people think I
am, not Sylvester Stallone.

00:04:36.813 --> 00:04:39.395
Most people, when I go
around the world, it's like,

00:04:39.395 --> 00:04:41.529
Hey Rocky, hey Rambo, it's not you.

00:04:41.529 --> 00:04:43.864
In one way it's very
flattering, you know, it's like,

00:04:43.864 --> 00:04:45.592
you've come up with
something that they enjoy,

00:04:45.592 --> 00:04:48.530
but I know that if I
gave them another Rocky,

00:04:48.530 --> 00:04:51.728
another Rambo all the time,
they would sour on it,

00:04:51.728 --> 00:04:53.818
you know, even though I do
things that aren't successful,

00:04:53.818 --> 00:04:56.485
the main thing in my work ethic,

00:04:58.067 --> 00:05:00.993
is you've got to take
chances, you've got to gamble,

00:05:00.993 --> 00:05:04.094
and if you win 51% of the
time, you've got it made.

00:05:04.094 --> 00:05:05.158
- What do you mean,
don't think about this,

00:05:05.158 --> 00:05:06.345
when you starting treatment?

00:05:06.345 --> 00:05:08.235
I'm not doing no chemotherapy.

00:05:08.235 --> 00:05:09.241
I'm not crazy at all.

00:05:09.241 --> 00:05:11.780
If I could take everything that was good,

00:05:11.780 --> 00:05:15.504
and put it into a bowl or
something, and say hey, here,

00:05:15.504 --> 00:05:20.290
I'd like to buy one more
day with my wife, I'd do it.

00:05:20.290 --> 00:05:23.957
Everything I got, is
moved on, and I'm here.

00:05:25.450 --> 00:05:27.655
I never wanted to do this movie.

00:05:27.655 --> 00:05:31.749
I thought, sick Rocky is so
counter-intuitive to what

00:05:31.749 --> 00:05:34.166
Rocky really is designed for.

00:05:35.453 --> 00:05:38.805
I just lay there, I said,
can someone else be sick

00:05:38.805 --> 00:05:41.739
in the movie and not me,
'cause I've never done that.

00:05:41.739 --> 00:05:43.547
My wife goes, "You're
a coward," and I went,

00:05:43.547 --> 00:05:45.002
"You know that's kind of a harsh word"

00:05:45.002 --> 00:05:47.652
he goes "No no, you're yellow
basically, you're a coward."

00:05:47.652 --> 00:05:51.569
It goes against every
undeclared artistic rule,

00:05:52.711 --> 00:05:55.955
if you're afraid of something,
that's the commitment

00:05:55.955 --> 00:06:00.834
of the artist, that's his
duty, to pursue the unknown,

00:06:00.834 --> 00:06:05.408
to go someplace where he's
literally at odds with himself.

00:06:05.408 --> 00:06:06.241
- [Adonis] "You all right there, old man?"

00:06:06.241 --> 00:06:08.468
- [Rocky] "Yeah."

00:06:08.468 --> 00:06:10.026
You know if you look hard enough,

00:06:10.026 --> 00:06:12.608
you can see your whole life from up here.

00:06:12.608 --> 00:06:14.404
- [Adonis] How does it look?

00:06:14.404 --> 00:06:15.987
- [Rocky] Not bad at all.

00:06:15.987 --> 00:06:18.423
- [Narrator] Stallone wrote a
screenplay for a boxing film

00:06:18.423 --> 00:06:21.828
called Rocky with himself as the lead.

00:06:21.828 --> 00:06:25.221
The studio loved the script,
but wanted Sly to step aside

00:06:25.221 --> 00:06:26.643
for a big name actor.

00:06:26.643 --> 00:06:31.174
Despite intense pressure,
Stallone refused to give in.

00:06:31.174 --> 00:06:34.798
- You have to try, you have
to see if you really are

00:06:34.798 --> 00:06:38.153
what you think you are,
and by that I mean,

00:06:38.153 --> 00:06:41.465
I wanted one chance to prove
whether I was a good actor,

00:06:41.465 --> 00:06:43.179
or that I was a lousy actor,
or whether I should go

00:06:43.179 --> 00:06:46.953
get a Dairy Queen stand
or what I should do,

00:06:46.953 --> 00:06:48.433
or even maybe I should get out of acting,

00:06:48.433 --> 00:06:50.586
and I just needed one vehicle to prove it.

00:06:50.586 --> 00:06:52.885
I had to be up there just enough to say,

00:06:52.885 --> 00:06:57.132
"Jesus, you stink
Stallone," or, "Not bad!"

00:06:57.132 --> 00:06:59.152
- [Narrator] The studio finally agreed.

00:06:59.152 --> 00:07:00.985
Sly gave it 100%.

00:07:02.240 --> 00:07:05.076
- I started about five
months into training,

00:07:05.076 --> 00:07:09.243
and I had a regime of
abstaining from hacky pracky,

00:07:10.432 --> 00:07:13.418
and eating a lot of meat, and developing

00:07:13.418 --> 00:07:17.867
a Tyrannosaurus Rex mentality,
running and sparring

00:07:17.867 --> 00:07:20.389
and taking the bruises, but I felt

00:07:20.389 --> 00:07:22.404
that that came out in the film.

00:07:22.404 --> 00:07:24.432
I knew this was my one shot
and I wasn't about to cheat

00:07:24.432 --> 00:07:25.694
on it, I wasn't about to come in there

00:07:25.694 --> 00:07:27.959
and look like Tinkerbell for
an hour and a half, I had this,

00:07:27.959 --> 00:07:31.445
"Oh God if I stink at least
let me skink with class!"

00:07:31.445 --> 00:07:34.358
Something, and geez, it was so great.

00:07:34.358 --> 00:07:36.878
In arm wrestling rules,
if you lift out of the cup

00:07:36.878 --> 00:07:40.392
like this, that does
disqualify, it disqualifies...

00:07:40.392 --> 00:07:41.454
- You had cheated.

00:07:41.454 --> 00:07:45.018
- Well let's just say I
lost my Australian rules.

00:07:45.018 --> 00:07:45.903
- [Derryn] Well let's have
a quick look at it again

00:07:45.903 --> 00:07:47.806
and just see how rough it really was.

00:07:47.806 --> 00:07:49.438
- [Sylvester] All right.

00:07:49.438 --> 00:07:52.885
Now, in arm wrestling the
elbow must remain on the table.

00:07:52.885 --> 00:07:54.276
Am I right?
- Evening up there, yeah.

00:07:54.276 --> 00:07:56.299
- Okay, now this man, here we go,

00:07:56.299 --> 00:07:58.869
and he's very strong, this guy is strong,

00:07:58.869 --> 00:08:00.994
all right here we go,

00:08:00.994 --> 00:08:03.117
he is hitting himself, the match is over,

00:08:03.117 --> 00:08:07.117
and now he is going north,
up up up up excuse me

00:08:08.074 --> 00:08:10.196
- [Derryn] You see he's
using his hand, his arm

00:08:10.196 --> 00:08:11.029
to lift his other arm.

00:08:11.029 --> 00:08:12.451
- [Sylvester] I mean,
I'm pointing, thank you,

00:08:12.451 --> 00:08:13.703
end of match.

00:08:13.703 --> 00:08:17.870
Now, we should cut the tape
at this point (laughing)

00:08:19.854 --> 00:08:22.134
- Not bad, but okay, even
at a time like that...

00:08:22.134 --> 00:08:24.226
- No, I got to say, this guy is strong,

00:08:24.226 --> 00:08:25.698
he's strong.
- But do you hate losing?

00:08:25.698 --> 00:08:28.891
- No, you see, I don't, I
don't, that's my philosophy,

00:08:28.891 --> 00:08:32.265
you go out, you try,
sometimes you get bad breaks,

00:08:32.265 --> 00:08:34.529
sometimes people don't play by the rules,

00:08:34.529 --> 00:08:37.129
whatever it is, but nah,
I'm not one of those people

00:08:37.129 --> 00:08:39.010
who are obsessed with it.

00:08:39.010 --> 00:08:40.760
I'm competitive, oh yeah,
I'm real competitive,

00:08:40.760 --> 00:08:44.927
but I've never been like
obsessed with, "I must go back."

00:08:46.635 --> 00:08:48.219
I like to try until the end,

00:08:48.219 --> 00:08:50.190
like if I'm working on a character,

00:08:50.190 --> 00:08:52.414
I want to push and push and
push until the breaking point

00:08:52.414 --> 00:08:56.385
but I've never been like in
sports where I have to go out,

00:08:56.385 --> 00:08:59.393
matter of fact, I play on a
football team, we had a ten game

00:08:59.393 --> 00:09:02.110
season, we were O and 10 for this season.

00:09:02.110 --> 00:09:02.974
O and 10.
- You lost 10.

00:09:02.974 --> 00:09:04.692
- And I was the captain, you
know what I mean, it's like,

00:09:04.692 --> 00:09:07.951
how do you get, so I'm used to it.

00:09:07.951 --> 00:09:11.071
Whenever you're saying Rocky,
I always feel as though

00:09:11.071 --> 00:09:14.485
we're giving a vote of confidence
for these great athletes,

00:09:14.485 --> 00:09:18.253
for real, you know I've never
pretended to be a boxer,

00:09:18.253 --> 00:09:22.672
I don't possess those skills,
but what I do think I have

00:09:22.672 --> 00:09:26.815
is an understanding of what
goes on outside the ring.

00:09:26.815 --> 00:09:30.608
Outside the ring is sometimes
maybe even a bigger struggle

00:09:30.608 --> 00:09:33.400
than what goes on inside the ring,

00:09:33.400 --> 00:09:36.340
and if I was able to capture that,

00:09:36.340 --> 00:09:38.787
then I believe you can
identify more with a fighter

00:09:38.787 --> 00:09:40.778
but more than that, we also realize

00:09:40.778 --> 00:09:42.768
that our life is a constant battle,

00:09:42.768 --> 00:09:45.593
sometimes I write things
in Rocky that may seem

00:09:45.593 --> 00:09:49.760
a little precious as they
say, or a little sentimental,

00:09:50.672 --> 00:09:54.785
but I truly believe it's
not how hard you can hit,

00:09:54.785 --> 00:09:58.158
it's how hard you can get
hit, and keep moving forward,

00:09:58.158 --> 00:10:01.162
because that's really what
does make the difference

00:10:01.162 --> 00:10:03.644
in your life, (audience
members cheering) you know.

00:10:03.644 --> 00:10:04.477
(audience applauds)

00:10:04.477 --> 00:10:05.786
It really does.

00:10:05.786 --> 00:10:07.350
You're all fantastic.

00:10:07.350 --> 00:10:11.165
These men here have always been
held in a special reverence

00:10:11.165 --> 00:10:13.712
for me, greatest athletes in
the world, but more than that,

00:10:13.712 --> 00:10:16.224
they are our connection to the past,

00:10:16.224 --> 00:10:18.449
and our way to the
future, they are the guys

00:10:18.449 --> 00:10:19.791
that go there and take the blows

00:10:19.791 --> 00:10:22.751
and show that if you really
put it out there on the line,

00:10:22.751 --> 00:10:24.334
you are a champion.

00:10:25.177 --> 00:10:26.629
You may not be the champion of the world

00:10:26.629 --> 00:10:28.182
but you'll be the champion of your life,

00:10:28.182 --> 00:10:30.265
and yo, Adrian, I did it!

00:10:31.511 --> 00:10:33.257
(audience cheers and applauds)

00:10:33.257 --> 00:10:37.695
I think that personal ambition
is worth fighting for,

00:10:37.695 --> 00:10:40.967
it really is something that
if you don't fight for it,

00:10:40.967 --> 00:10:42.666
you're going to regret it
for the rest of your life,

00:10:42.666 --> 00:10:44.677
and if you regret it, you
could be an unhappy person,

00:10:44.677 --> 00:10:46.667
if you're an unhappy person
it can affect your family,

00:10:46.667 --> 00:10:49.875
so you can see the chain of
command all the way down,

00:10:49.875 --> 00:10:53.120
it can be pretty devastating.

00:10:53.120 --> 00:10:56.066
The common answer is we
fight for family, yeah,

00:10:56.066 --> 00:10:59.399
but fighting for family starts with you,

00:11:00.357 --> 00:11:03.114
so you got to fight for peace
of mind, that's what I think,

00:11:03.114 --> 00:11:07.031
you have to go for, what
makes you happy enough

00:11:08.378 --> 00:11:10.944
in your life that you want
to make other people happy?

00:11:10.944 --> 00:11:12.560
I don't know about anyone
else, but I really feel

00:11:12.560 --> 00:11:13.967
it's a privilege to be here tonight,

00:11:13.967 --> 00:11:16.952
and I'm going to try my best to, what?

00:11:16.952 --> 00:11:19.217
(audience laughing and cheering)

00:11:19.217 --> 00:11:21.050
- You stole my script!

00:11:21.890 --> 00:11:24.158
You stole my script, don't you dare--

00:11:24.158 --> 00:11:25.364
(audience cheering and applauding)

00:11:25.364 --> 00:11:28.350
No, I'm sorry, I watched the
movie, you stole my script,

00:11:28.350 --> 00:11:29.231
all that was me--

00:11:29.231 --> 00:11:31.445
- You been puttin' me on for years, Ali--

00:11:31.445 --> 00:11:34.680
- Show me what you're going to
do, show me what you can do!

00:11:34.680 --> 00:11:35.702
- Know my real name, doncha?

00:11:35.702 --> 00:11:39.869
(audience laughing and applauding)

00:11:56.141 --> 00:11:57.661
- Thank you guys so much for watching,

00:11:57.661 --> 00:11:59.910
I'd love to know what did
you take from this video,

00:11:59.910 --> 00:12:02.834
what was the most important
lesson that you learned,

00:12:02.834 --> 00:12:05.180
that blew your mind, that
you're going to immediately

00:12:05.180 --> 00:12:08.017
apply to your life or
your business somehow,

00:12:08.017 --> 00:12:10.008
please leave it down
in the comments below,

00:12:10.008 --> 00:12:11.036
I'm super curious to find out.

00:12:11.036 --> 00:12:12.296
Also if you want to nominate someone

00:12:12.296 --> 00:12:15.415
for the next top ten video,
please check the description

00:12:15.415 --> 00:12:17.750
for a link to a video where
you can vote for people

00:12:17.750 --> 00:12:19.851
and put in your suggestions as well.

00:12:19.851 --> 00:12:21.885
I also want to give a quick
shout out to Bailey Cooper,

00:12:21.885 --> 00:12:24.599
thank you so much Bailey for
picking up a copy of my book,

00:12:24.599 --> 00:12:27.242
Your One Word, and putting
it in your YouTube video,

00:12:27.242 --> 00:12:28.857
I really appreciate the support man,

00:12:28.857 --> 00:12:30.512
and I'm glad you're enjoying the read.

00:12:30.512 --> 00:12:33.973
- Your One Word, by Evan Carmichael,

00:12:33.973 --> 00:12:37.006
and I strongly recommend this book.

00:12:37.006 --> 00:12:38.816
- So thank you guys again for watching,

00:12:38.816 --> 00:12:41.329
I believe in you, I hope
you continue to believe

00:12:41.329 --> 00:12:43.773
in yourself, and whatever,
your one word is,

00:12:43.773 --> 00:12:46.883
much love, I'll see you soon.

00:12:46.883 --> 00:12:48.966
(swoosh)

00:12:52.917 --> 00:12:55.957
- If I didn't make it as
an actor, writer, painter,

00:12:55.957 --> 00:13:00.538
I would have gone into
something in the physical vein,

00:13:00.538 --> 00:13:03.161
something where, I would have
liked to have been a coach

00:13:03.161 --> 00:13:07.171
of some sort, because I enjoy
motivating a great deal,

00:13:07.171 --> 00:13:08.171
I really do.

00:13:09.108 --> 00:13:10.806
I like to motivate.

00:13:10.806 --> 00:13:11.639
- Everybody around you.

00:13:11.639 --> 00:13:12.806
- Yes, I do.

00:13:12.806 --> 00:13:15.434
I've been discovered, I've
been around for a while,

00:13:15.434 --> 00:13:18.920
all I want to do is get a
certain kind of momentum going

00:13:18.920 --> 00:13:23.344
and do films that I'm not
ashamed of or really disappoint

00:13:23.344 --> 00:13:26.307
my audience, you know,
I'm not the new young kid

00:13:26.307 --> 00:13:28.998
on the block by any means,
I've been around quite a while,

00:13:28.998 --> 00:13:31.915
that's all, I just want to pick up,

00:13:32.976 --> 00:13:35.870
I feel like George
Foreman, he kind of left

00:13:35.870 --> 00:13:38.787
on a kind of dubious
note, I want to come back

00:13:38.787 --> 00:13:41.983
and do the things that I
do best and really push it

00:13:41.983 --> 00:13:43.971
as far as humanly possible that I can do,

00:13:43.971 --> 00:13:45.648
I like the challenge, that's all.

00:13:45.648 --> 00:13:49.815
If people were to say that
the money at a certain point

00:13:52.431 --> 00:13:55.764
is not important, I think they would be,

00:13:57.617 --> 00:13:58.868
I think they would be reveling

00:13:58.868 --> 00:14:02.623
in a serious case of mendacity,
(laughs) I believe that

00:14:02.623 --> 00:14:05.148
when you get to a
certain level and you see

00:14:05.148 --> 00:14:08.967
one performer is getting
a number right away,

00:14:08.967 --> 00:14:12.467
you feel as though, okay, to be respected,

00:14:13.638 --> 00:14:15.428
it becomes a numbers game.

00:14:15.428 --> 00:14:18.177
I think more importantly
it is to the agent,

00:14:18.177 --> 00:14:21.229
than quite often it is to
the actor, for example,

00:14:21.229 --> 00:14:25.664
in the film I just completed
I was paid nothing, zero.

00:14:25.664 --> 00:14:26.497
- That's Cop Land.

00:14:26.497 --> 00:14:27.899
- Absolutely nothing, I mean...

00:14:27.899 --> 00:14:29.595
- You'll get some back in profit if it--

00:14:29.595 --> 00:14:31.160
- If it does, you gamble.
- If it does well.

00:14:31.160 --> 00:14:34.977
- But you see, that to
me is, I've never been,

00:14:34.977 --> 00:14:36.560
quote, a mercenary,

00:14:39.912 --> 00:14:41.021
at one time I thought I was,

00:14:41.021 --> 00:14:43.651
but it's not about money,
otherwise I wouldn't waive this,

00:14:43.651 --> 00:14:44.946
and I would take the safe route--

00:14:44.946 --> 00:14:47.606
- And it's not about buying
more art or buying more cars

00:14:47.606 --> 00:14:48.902
or buying more homes,
- No, no no,

00:14:48.902 --> 00:14:49.735
no, no, no.
- Or any of that stuff,

00:14:49.735 --> 00:14:51.270
You're way beyond that.

00:14:51.270 --> 00:14:55.437
- No, really, I have all the
material comforts one needs,

00:14:56.375 --> 00:15:00.876
now it's all about the, (sigh)

00:15:00.876 --> 00:15:03.454
the library of memories you leave behind.

00:15:03.454 --> 00:15:04.340
- The body of work.

00:15:04.340 --> 00:15:05.673
- Exactly right.

